      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-22-2022-june/q1",
      "question": "<p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.8\\text{ m}\"></span> vertically above horizontal ground.</p><p>At time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t = 0\"></span>, a small stone is projected vertically upwards with speed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"U\\text{ m s}^{-1}\"></span> from the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>.</p><p>At time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t = T\"></span> seconds, the stone hits the ground.</p><p>The speed of the stone as it hits the ground is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\\text{ m s}^{-1}\"></span></p><p>In an initial model of the motion of the stone as it moves from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> to where it hits the ground</p><ul><li>the stone is modelled as a particle moving freely under gravity</li></ul><ul><li>the acceleration due to gravity is modelled as having magnitude <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\\text{ m s}^{-2}\"></span></li></ul><p>Using the model,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"U\"></span>,</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Suggest one refinement, apart from including air resistance, that would make the model more realistic.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>In reality the stone will not move freely under gravity and will be subject to air resistance.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(d) Explain how this would affect your answer to part (a).</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
