      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-22-2022-june/q2",
      "question": "<p>A train travels along a straight horizontal track from station <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> to station <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span>.</p><p>In a model of the motion of the train, at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t = 0\"></span> the train starts from rest at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>, and moves with constant acceleration until it reaches its maximum speed of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"25 \\text{ m s}^{-1}\"></span></p><p>The train then travels at this constant speed of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"25 \\text{ m s}^{-1}\"></span> before finally moving with constant deceleration until it comes to rest at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span>.</p><p>The time spent decelerating is four times the time spent accelerating.</p><p>The journey from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span> takes 700 s.</p><p>Using the model,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) sketch a speed-time graph for the motion of the train between the two stations <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>The distance between the two stations is 15 km.</p><p>Using the model,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) show that the time spent accelerating by the train is 40 s,</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) find the acceleration, in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\text{m s}^{-2}\"></span>, of the train,</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(d) find the speed of the train 572 s after leaving <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(e) State one limitation of the model which could affect your answers to parts (b) and (c).</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
